{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00078","versions":[{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00078","release":"R19-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00078","release":"R20-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00078","release":"R21-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00078","release":"R22-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00078@rel:R23-11#f3901c3e","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00078","release":"R23-11","content":"[SWS_SecOC_00078]⌈\nDuring reception of an (Secured / Authentic / Cryptographic) I-PDU by means of a\nlower layer bus interface and when SecOC_RxIndication has been called, the\nSecOC module shall copy the I-PDU into the according buffer according to the\nminimum of received length and configured length of this I-PDU. The copied length\nshall then be used for all further reception processings.\n⌋(SRS_SecOC_00010, SRS_SecOC_00012, SRS_SecOC_00013)\nNote: Copying only minimum of configured and passed length ensures that buffer cannot be\noverwritten and that non-expected data (which was maybe added due to padding) is discarded. For\nreception from TP this restriction is not needed as TP ensures a valid length value passed. For\ndynamic length PDUs with a shorter length than configured only the length provided will be copied.\nAlso for dynamic length PDUs TPS_SYST_02189 ensures that a reliable length information is\navailable.\nThereafter, the actual verification of anincoming Secured I-PDU is initiated during\nthe next call of the scheduled main function. The SecOC module extracts the\nAuthentic I-PDU, the Authentication Information from the Secured I-PDU. The SecOC\nmodule verifies the authenticity and freshness of the Authentic I-PDU according to\nSecOC_SWS_0040. If the verification is successful, the SecOC indicates the\nreception of the Authentic I-PDU by calling PduR_SecOC[If|Tp]RxIndication\nfor the Authentic I-PDU. If the verification fails, the SecOC drops the PDU and does\nnot call PduR_SecOC[If|Tp]RxIndication.","meta":{"source_pdf":"SWS_SecureOnboardCommunication.pdf","source_page":52,"trigger_kind":"snippet_ingest"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-04T00:00:00+00:00","text_key":"10de0e544b0e","rejoin":{"rule":"text-rejoin@1","e":[[18,1," "],[99,1," "],[174,1," "],[251,1," "],[333,1," "],[444,1," "],[533,1," "],[629,1," "],[725,1," "],[824,1," "],[914,1," "],[925,1," "],[1009,1," "],[1085,1," "],[1167,1," "],[1250,1," "],[1325,1," "],[1399,1," "],[1484,1," "]]}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00078","release":"R24-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00078","release":"R25-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00078","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R19-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":[],"platform_releases":["R18-10","R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11","text_releases":["R23-11"],"presence_only":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"unchecked":["R18-10"]},"element":{"kind":"requirement","name":"","module":"SecOC","cluster":"security","page":"","doc_type":"SWS","ai":false,"first":"R19-11","last":"R25-11","changed":[],"distinct":1,"universe":"CP"},"evidence":{"figures":[{"id":"FIG-b2873332d2b34f95","doc":"AUTOSAR_SWS_SecureOnboardCommunication","p":100,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.9,"rt":"SEQU